It suddenly occurs to me - why not be able to throw things down a
staircase before descending, as one could do in real life?  Potions
and cameras, of course, would break (unless they were in a well-packed
bag, when there might be a percentage chance of breakage), and you'd
get no potion effect since they'd be breaking on a different level.

This way, you could just step over the cockatrice corpse on
descending.  Of course, if there were a glove-wearing nasty (like a
soldier) on the floor below, you'd be in trouble...  Unless the
soldier-type were *directly* below, so if it got hit, you'd descend to
find the cockatrice corpse and a petrified soldier.  Still, a risky
venture.  

This train of thought engenders a question:  If you're completely
covered with armor, wouldn't (or shouldn't) you be protected from the
petrifying aspect of getting hit with a cockatrice corpse (though not
from any damage it would do from a heavy *thump* on your noggin)?

